185
00:13:45,408 --> 00:13:48,277
in exercises/m19-m25-github.md.

186
00:13:52,117 --> 00:13:56,626
Answer out loud. The question fixes the
form: four mechanisms, four commands.

187
00:13:56,666 --> 00:14:01,292
A strong answer begins with what the page
computes, so that the four mechanisms

188
00:14:01,332 --> 00:14:06,136
follow from it instead of being recited:
something about the base, something about

189
00:14:06,176 --> 00:14:11,098
the head's ancestry, something about a
rewrite, something about content that changed

190
00:14:11,138 --> 00:14:11,925
on every line.

191
00:14:12,265 --> 00:14:16,802
Each command is one that the developer can
run in their own clone, and for each you

192
00:14:16,842 --> 00:14:21,323
say what output confirms the mechanism.
Add the order in which you would test them

193
00:14:21,363 --> 00:14:25,183
and why, and one sentence on which
repairs keep the pull request open.

194
00:14:27,023 --> 00:14:27,950
Let's land this.

195
00:14:28,290 --> 00:14:33,011
A pull request lists everything reachable
from the head and not from the base, and

196
00:14:33,051 --> 00:14:35,740
shows the diff from the
merge base to the head.

197
00:14:36,080 --> 00:14:40,671
A sudden jump in size means the head,
the base or the merge base changed; each

198
00:14:40,711 --> 00:14:42,868
candidate has a read-only local test.

199
00:14:43,208 --> 00:14:48,185
A merge of another branch into the head
brings all of that branch's commits into the

200
00:14:48,225 --> 00:14:48,962
pull request.

201
00:14:49,302 --> 00:14:54,360
A reverted merge is not a removed merge:
the ancestry stays, and a later merge of

202
00:14:54,400 --> 00:14:56,059
that branch brings nothing.

203
00:14:56,399 --> 00:15:01,460
The repair for a single-author topic branch
is a rebuild with git rebase --onto, a

204
00:15:01,500 --> 00:15:02,953
lease, and a new review.

205
00:15:04,793 --> 00:15:10,732
Read section 30.10. Then generate Incident
7, incidents/07-ci-passes-locally, read

206
00:15:10,772 --> 00:15:16,638
its evidence directory together with the
symptoms, and attempt it before the next

207
00:15:16,678 --> 00:15:17,076
video.

208
00:15:17,416 --> 00:15:22,434
You can now find why a pull request grew
overnight, and rebuild its branch without

209
00:15:22,474 --> 00:15:27,554
